      "nets": ["MAX3485 DE/RE node"],
      "observed": "U2 pins 2 and 3 (RE/DE) are tied together and driven by Q1's collector, but no resistor is connected from that node to GND or +3V3. The only bias/pull resistors shown around U2 are R23=2k, R18=2.2k, and R14=2.2k on the A/B lines.",
      "expected": "The specification calls for a 20 kΩ resistor as part of the MAX3485 DE/RE bias/pull network (R6, R7, R8, R15 = 2k, 20k, 2.2k, 2.2k).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R6, R7, R8, R15 | 2k, 20k, 2.2k, 2.2k | Bias/pull network on the MAX3485 A/B differential lines and DE/RE enable line."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U2 MAX3485 pins 2/3 (RE/DE) to Q1; R23 2k, R18 2.2k, R14 2.2k; no 20k resistor drawn"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When Q1 is off, the MAX3485 enable pins can float, leaving the transceiver's driver/receiver state undefined. In serial mode this can cause unreliable communication or bus contention.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J9", "D2", "Q3"],
      "pins": ["J9.1", "D2.anode", "Q3.source"],
      "nets": ["5V_POWER", "+5V", "NET0041"],
      "observed": "The 5V_POWER input connector J9 pin 1 is wired to both D2 (SS54) and the source of Q3 (IRLML6402); D2's cathode is +5V and Q3's drain is NET0041, the M5Stack /BAT bus net.",
      "expected": "The specification requires a separate battery input (J5) connected only to Q1's source, and a separate external 5V input (J7) connected only through D1 to the +5V rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The battery connects at J5, through Q1 ... onto the /BAT net ... J7 (labelled 5V_POWER) feeds the board's +5V rail through D1 (SS54)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "J9 5V_POWER pin 1 -> D2 SS54 -> +5V; same pin 1 wire also connects to Q3 IRLML6402; Q3 drain -> NET0041"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Closing the optional switch can apply the external 5V input to the M5Stack BAT pin, bypassing the intended battery/charging path and potentially damaging the Core or causing unexpected power-up. The intended separate battery disconnect path is not implemented.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic deviates from the specification: the required 20 kΩ MAX3485 DE/RE bias resistor is absent, and the 5V_POWER input appears merged with the switched /BAT path instead of using separate battery and external-5V connectors."
}

